## Object Validations

### Object Type
```javascript
body('address')
  .isObject()
  .withMessage('Address must be an object')
```

### Nested Object Validation
```javascript
// Address object with nested validation
body('address')
  .isObject()
  .custom((address) => {
    const requiredFields = ['street', 'city', 'zipCode'];
    const missing = requiredFields.filter(field => !address[field]);

    if (missing.length > 0) {
      throw new Error(`Address missing fields: ${missing.join(', ')}`);
    }

    if (!/\d{5}/.test(address.zipCode)) {
      throw new Error('Invalid zip code format');
    }

    return true;
  })

// Or use separate validations for nested fields
body('address.street').notEmpty()
body('address.city').notEmpty()
body('address.zipCode').matches(/^\d{5}$/)
```

