## Best Practices

### 1. Always Validate on the Server
```javascript
// ❌ Don't rely only on client-side validation
// ✅ Always validate on the server regardless of client validation
```

### 2. Use Whitelist Validation
```javascript
// ❌ Bad - blacklist approach (too many possibilities)
body('username').not().matches(/admin/)

// ✅ Good - whitelist approach (only allow valid characters)
body('username').matches(/^[a-zA-Z0-9_]{3,30}$/)
```

### 3. Sanitize Input
```javascript
// Always escape output
res.json({ name: escapeHtml(user.name) });
```

### 4. Use Descriptive Error Messages
```javascript
// ❌ Bad
.withMessage('Invalid input')

// ✅ Good
.withMessage('Username must be 3-30 alphanumeric characters')
```

### 5. Validate Before Business Logic
```javascript
// Validate first, then process
const validationResults = validationResult(req);
if (!validationResults.isEmpty()) {
  return res.status(400).json({ errors: validationResults.array() });
}
// Now safe to process the data
```

### 6. Keep Validation Simple and Testable
```javascript
// Write validation rules that are easy to test
body('email')
  .trim()
  .isEmail()
  .normalizeEmail()
```

